//! Indicator reference fixtures over a realistic deterministic 150-bar OHLCV series.
//!
//! Every expected value was computed by a standalone script that does not use this crate, by
//! transcribing the published formula definitions:
//!
//! - TradingView Pine v5 reference manual: `ta.ema`/`ta.rma` (`na(sum[1]) ? ta.sma(src, length) :
//!   alpha * src + (1 - alpha) * nz(sum[1])`), `ta.rsi`, `ta.macd`, `ta.stdev` (biased), `ta.bb`,
//!   `ta.stoch` and the built-in Stochastic (%K smoothing 1, %D = `ta.sma(%K, 3)`).
//! - 通达信/同花顺 formula language: `EMA(X,N)` `Y=(2*X+(N-1)*Y')/(N+1)` and `SMA(X,N,M)`
//!   `Y=(M*X+(N-M)*Y')/N`, both seeded by the first valid `X`; `MACD` (`DIF`, `DEA`,
//!   `(DIF-DEA)*2`); `RSI` `SMA(MAX(C-LC,0),N,1)/SMA(ABS(C-LC),N,1)*100`; `BOLL`
//!   `MA(C,20) ± 2*STD(C,20)` with the sample `STD`.
//! - Textbook KDJ (东方财富百科 "随机指标"): 9-day RSV, `K = 2/3 K' + 1/3 RSV`,
//!   `D = 2/3 D' + 1/3 K`, `J = 3K - 2D`, with 50 standing in for the missing previous K and D.
//!
//! Each fixture pins the leading 40 rows (where seed conventions differ) and the last 5 rows.
//! `NAN` marks a row where the definition has no value yet. Both the dense functions and the
//! incremental runtime (full rebuild and bar-by-bar streaming) must reproduce them.

